    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d88">

                <pb facs="0090" n="768" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg768"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Dayton</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 395.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 11, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 27th of August (No.
                    338) has been received. You will inform Mr. Drouyn de l’Huys that his prompt,
                    efficient, and friendly proceedings in regard to the ram which is being built at
                    Liverpool are appreciated by the President.</p>
                <pb facs="0091" n="769" xml:id="pg769"/>
                <p>I regret to say that reports of our consul at Liverpool leave little room to
                    doubt that Mr. Bravay’s pretences to interfere in regard to these vessels, as an
                    agent from the Pacha of Egypt, are false and fraudulent. The consul writes that
                    he had telegraphed to the consul general at Alexandria, and so it is probable
                    that the truth will be ascertained. Should Mr. Bravay be proved to have been
                    engaged in an attempt to deceive the French government, you will doubtless make
                    a proper representation of the case.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> L. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dayton</hi>, Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
